# GATE 1 — code review (POC-PLAN.md §9).
#
# The App Owner / Dev Lead persona reviews every AI-authored patch here.  Ba0Ba0's
# in-app code-review approval posts a real GitHub PR review as this reviewer, which is
# what makes Gate 1 a genuine block rather than a screen.
#
# Replace BAOBAO_ORG with the confirmed org name (POC-PLAN.md Prerequisites, item 1).

*                       @BAOBAO_ORG/app-owners

# Security-sensitive paths get the security team as well.  app/jobs/archive.py holds
# the seeded CWE-22, and POC-PLAN.md §7 makes human review of SAST fixes mandatory —
# never auto-merge a logic change.
/app/jobs/archive.py    @BAOBAO_ORG/app-owners @BAOBAO_ORG/sec
/tests/security/        @BAOBAO_ORG/app-owners @BAOBAO_ORG/sec

# The seed manifest defines what the demo is supposed to find.  Changing it changes the
# acceptance criteria, so it needs the security team's eyes.
/.baobao/               @BAOBAO_ORG/sec

# Patch targets for the mechanical channels.  Dependency and base-image bumps are the
# routine path; they still need an owner's approval, which is the point of Gate 1.
/Dockerfile             @BAOBAO_ORG/app-owners
/requirements.txt       @BAOBAO_ORG/app-owners

# Pipeline changes are infra's call, and the AI patch agent's file allowlist forbids it
# from touching CI config at all (POC-PLAN.md §7 guardrails).
/.github/               @BAOBAO_ORG/infra
